hadiths[51]{hadithnumber,text}:
"727","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me, ""Mention Allah's Name (i.e., say Bismillah before starting eating), eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"728","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When any of you wants to eat, he should mention the Name of Allah in the begining, (i.e., say Bismillah). If he forgets to do it in the beginning, he should say Bismillah awwalahu wa akhirahu (I begin with the Name of Allah at the beginning and at the end)."" [At-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawud] ."
"729","I heard Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, ""If a person mentions the Name of Allah upon entering his house or eating, Satan says, addressing his followers: 'You will find no where to spend the night and no dinner.' But if he enters without mentioning the Name of Allah, Satan says (to his followers); 'You have found (a place) to spend the night in, and if he does not mention the Name of Allah at the time of eating, Satan says: 'You have found (a place) to spend the night in as well as food.""' [Muslim] ."
"730","On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When we attended a meal with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we would not place our hands on the food until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) placed his hand first. And once we attended a meal with him, and a maid came as if she was pushing, so she went to put her hand in the food, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took her hand. Then a Bedouin came as if pushing, so the Prophet took his [the Bedouin's] hand, then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: He said: “The devil makes food permissible if the name of Allah Almighty is not mentioned on it, and he brought this slave girl to make it permissible for her, so I took her by the hand, and he brought this Bedouin to make it permissible for him [the Bedouin], so I took his hand, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, his hand is in my hand along with their hands.” Then he mentioned the name of Allah Almighty and ate. [Muslim]"
"731","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting while a man was eating food. That man did not mention the Name of Allah (before commencing to eat) till only a morsel of food was left. When he raised it to his mouth, he said: ""Bismillah awwalahu wa akhirahu (With the Name of Allah, in the beginning and in the end)."" Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) smiled at this and said, ""Satan had been eating with him but when he mentioned the Name of Allah, Satan vomited all that was in his stomach."" [Abu Dawud and An-Nasa'i] ."
"732","On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was eating food with six of his companions, and a Bedouin came and ate it in two bites. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “If it had been named, it would have been enough for you.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"733","And on the authority of Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet (ﷺ) would raise his table, he would say: “Praise be to Allah, abundant praise, good and blessed, not sufficient, not consigned, and not without Him. [Al-Bukhari]"
"734","On the authority of Muadh bin Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever eats food and says: Praise be to Allah who fed me this, and provided me with it without my power or strength, his previous sins will be forgiven.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"735","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never criticized food. If he desired it, he ate it, and if he disliked it, he left it.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"736","And on the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) asked his family about the condiment, and they said: We only have vinegar. So he called for it, and started eating and saying: “How excellent is the condiment, vinegar, how excellent is the condiment, vinegar.” [Muslim]"
"737","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When any of you is invited to a meal, he should accept the invitation. If he is observing Saum (fasting), he should supplicate, and if he is not fasting, he should eat."" [Muslim] ."
"738","On the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man called the Prophet (ﷺ) to eat food that the fifth of five people had prepared for him. A man followed them, and when he reached the door, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “This one has followed us; if you wish, you may give him permission, and if you wish, he may return.” He said: Rather, give him permission, O Messenger of Allah. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"739","I was a boy under the care of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and as my hand used to wander around in the dish, he (ﷺ) said to me once, ""Mention Allah's Name (i.e., say Bismillah), eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"740","On the authority of Salama bin Al-Akwa’, that a man ate with the Messenger of Allah with his left hand, and he said: “Eat with your right hand.” He said: I cannot. He said: “No, you can’t!” Nothing prevented him except arrogance! He did not raise it to his mouth. [Muslim]"
"741","On the authority of Jablah bin Suhaim, who said: We had a year of famine with Ibn al-Zubayr, and we were provided with dates. Abdullah bin Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, would pass by us while we were eating, and he would say: Do not pair, for the Prophet forbade pairing, then he would say: “Unless the man asks his brother’s permission” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"742","On the authority of Wahshi bin Harb, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: O Messenger of Allah, we eat and are not satisfied. He said: “Perhaps you eat separately (i.e. do not gather together for your meals).” They said: Yes. He said: So gather around for your food, and mention the name of Allah. He will bless you in it. [Abu Dawud]"
"743","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its edges and do not eat from its middle.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]"
"744","On the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) had a bowl called: Al-Ghara, carried by four men. When they sacrificed the sacrifice and performed the Duha (mid-morning) prayer, he brought that bowl, meaning he had crumbled bread into it, so they gathered around him, and when many people had gathered, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) knelt down. A Bedouin said: What is this sitting? The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Allah made me a generous servant, and He did not make me a stubborn tyrant. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Eat from around it, and leave its peaks to be blessed.” [Abu Dawud]"
"745","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""I do not eat reclining (against a pillow)."" [Al-Bukhari] ."
"746","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sitting on his knees eating dates. [Muslim]"
"747","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When one of you finishes eating, he should not wipe his fingers until he has licked them himself or has given them to someone else to lick for him."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"748","On the authority of Ka’b bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) eating with three fingers, and when he finished, he licked them. [Muslim]"
"749","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded licking the fingers and the dish, and said: “You do not know in which of your food the blessing lies.” [Muslim]"
"750","On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a morsel of one of you falls, let him take it and remove any impurity that is on it and eat it, and do not leave it for the devil, and do not wipe his hand with a napkin until he licks his fingers, for he does not know in which food his food is blessed.” [Muslim]"
"751","And on his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The devil is present with one of you in everything that concerns him, even when he eats. If a morsel of one of you falls, let him take it and remove any dirt that was on it, then let him eat it and not leave it for the devil. When he finishes, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which food his food is blessed.” [Muslim]"
"752","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ate food, he would lick his three fingers and say: “If a morsel of one of you falls, let him take it, remove the dirt from it, and eat it, and not leave it to the devil.” He commanded us to scrape the bowl clean and said: “You do not know in which of your food the blessing lies.” [Muslim]"
"753","I asked Jabir (May Allah be pleased with him) whether it was obligatory to make Wudu' for Salat (prayer) after eating cooked food. He said: ""No, because in the lifetime of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) such food was rarely available. We had no handkerchiefs, so when we ate such food we would wipe our fingers against our palms, forearms or (the sole of our) feet, and would offer Salat without fresh Wudu' (for prayer)."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
"754","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The food of two is sufficient for three, and the food of three is sufficient for four.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"755","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The food of one person suffices for two, the food of two persons suffices for four persons, and the food of four persons suffices for eight persons."" [Muslim] ."
"756","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to sip three drinks. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"757","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not drink one thing like a camel drinks, but drink two and three, and mention the name of Allah when you drink, and praise Allah when you finish.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"758","The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade breathing into the vessel while drinking. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"759","Milk mixed with water was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). On his right side was sitting a bedouin and on his left was sitting Abu Bakr (May Allah be pleased with him). He (ﷺ) drank from it and handed the rest to the bedouin saying, ""One who is on the right has preference, then again the one who is on the right."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"760","A drink was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he drank (some) from it. On his right was a boy and on his left were some elderly people. He (ﷺ) said to the boy, ""Would you permit me to give rest of this drink to these on my left?"" The boy said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I would certainly not give preference to anyone in anything that might come to me from you."" So he (ﷺ) handed over the rest of the drink to him. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"761","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah forbade breaking the mouths of water-skins, and drinking from them. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"762","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin or leather container. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"763","On the authority of Umm Thabit Kabsha bint Thabit, the sister of Hassan bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him and her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me and drank from a water skin hanging while standing, so I got up and cut it off [Al-Tirmidhi]. Rather, she cut it to preserve the place of the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and to seek blessing from it and protect it from vulgarity. This hadith is interpreted as an explanation of permissibility, and the previous two hadiths are an explanation of what is better and more complete, and Allah knows best."
"764","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited us blowing in the drinking water. A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Sometimes I see some litter floating about on the surface. What should I do then?"" He (ﷺ) replied, ""Pour them out."" Then the man said: ""My thirst is not quenched with one draught."" Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Then put away the cup from your mouth (in between three gulps), and take breath."" [At-Tirmidhi] ."
"765","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade breathing into a vessel, or blowing into it. [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"766","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I gave the Prophet (ﷺ) water to drink from Zamzam, and he drank while standing. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"767","On the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, came to Bab Al-Rahba and drank while standing, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do as you saw me do. [Al-Bukhari]"
"768","On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them, he said: During the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we used to eat while walking, and drink while standing. [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"769","On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drinking standing or sitting. [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"770","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he forbade a man from drinking while standing. Qatada said: So we said to Anas: What about eating? He said: That is more evil - or more insidious. And in his narration, the Prophet (ﷺ) discouraged drinking while standing. [Muslim] And in his narration, the Prophet (ﷺ) discouraged drinking while standing."
"771","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “None of you should drink while standing, so whoever forgets, let him vomit.” [Muslim]"
"772","On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “The server of the people is the last of them to drink.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"773","Once the time for As-Salat (the prayer) approached. Those whose houses were near, went to their houses (to perform Wudu') while some of the people remained with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). A stone (containing some water) bowl was brought for him. It was too small for him to spread his hand over it. He performed his Wudu' and it (the water) sufficed for all the others also. Anas was asked: ""How many of you were present there?"" He said: ""Eighty or more."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. This is Al-Bukhari's version. In Muslim's version ""'that Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) called for a container of water so he was given a vessel that had some water.' Anas said 'Then I started looking at the water spouting from his fingers. Then I estimated (the persons) and they were between seventy and eighty.'"""
"774","The Prophet (ﷺ) visited us and we brought water for him in a brass vessel for his ablution and he performed ablution. [Al- Bukhari] ."
"775","On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon a man from the Ansar, and with him was a friend of his, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If you have water, spend the night this night in a year, otherwise we drank (without it)” [Al-Bukhari]"
"776","The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited us from wearing brocade or silk and drinking out of gold or silver vessels and said, ""These are meant for them (disbelievers) in this world and for you in the Hereafter."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"777","On the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever drinks from vessels of silver will only drag fire from Hell in his stomach.”"
